Experimental explicit restricted-startup SDK ownership; not applied by Context Foundry.
Target: can1357/oh-my-pi @ 24439066040e006eb08da7b204f0ac41c79d2de9
Owner: 003 T006, bounded-pilot-v2 startup observation and admission.
Requires omp-startup-connection-warmups.patch and omp-startup-auth-retirement.patch.
The qualified source host also includes omp-startup-refusal.patch.
Modules: coding-agent main.ts::buildSessionOptions/loadTrustedSessionExtensions,
sdk.ts::createAgentSession/sealRestrictedStartup, startup-connection-warmups.ts.
Tests: startup-connection-warmups.test.ts and cli-restricted-startup.test.ts.
Difference: opt-in --restrict-tools requires explicit --tools; restricted startup
binds only explicitly trusted prepared extension factories to the real SDK session.
The one-use identity seal proves tool/MCP/memory restrictions and joining the original
credential-usage prefetch. Ordinary --tools keeps its existing behavior.
Five original connection warm-up owners and their original observer are preserved.
This does not close every startup owner, grant Ready, enable capture, authorize
paid execution, or establish complete network interception. No release signing.
Qualification and intentional limits: docs/validation.md, restricted startup inventory.

